{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"scripts/inspect-finding.py\n=== ===\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"REFERENCE PROTOTYPE, NOT A SHIPPED TOOL — for the \"scan findings are not\ninspectable enough to act on\" item in docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md.\n\nKept because it was validated against a real blocked sync: a 26 KB\nconversation turn where the 20-char excerpt could not distinguish a discussion\nof `getInput(\"github-token\")` from an actual leak. Python only because it was\na throwaway; the real feature belongs in src/redact/ beside `formatFinding`.\n\nTwo things to carry into the real implementation:\n  1. Searching by a needle copied out of the excerpt, as this does, is a\n     workaround for `Finding` not carrying the JSON path that `walkStrings`\n     already computes and hands to `visit`. Carry the path instead.\n  2. The unmasked region must go to a file, never stdout — an agent session\n     watching the terminal would re-capture the secret into a new event,\n     which is the same feedback loop `buildExcerpt`'s masking exists to stop.\n\nOriginal working notes follow.\n\n`cledger sync` prints ~20 chars around a match with the secret itself masked,\nwhich is often too little to judge a false positive, and there is no built-in\nway to see the raw event. This dumps the flagged event from `cledger export`\n(lossless) and shows a wide window around each match.\n\nSAFETY: the output contains the UNMASKED secret. By default it writes to a file","is_error":false,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WkE76uhD2KNuNPKUr3mjur","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","dirty_fingerprint":"bbe20560a71a254635cbd033aa353a00fbd2c3fb094525003f36b4423871768b","head":"183e3e0941068e8524d568b98297e3439d058c1f","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:cef69ec2-8b5a-4e91-8078-ac9